+# draft-person-date-of-birth: Add a date of birth to the person
+
+- **Jira:** none yet (direct request)
+- **Gate:** normal
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:**
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: none
+
+## Context
+
+A person can give a date of birth when they register. The identity module stores it and returns it with the person record.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+No Discovery AC covers the date of birth. The requirements of the request, tested in `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts`:
+
+| Requirement | Test |
+|---|---|
+| `registerPerson` accepts an optional `dateOfBirth` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) | "stores the date of birth and returns it" |
+| `getPerson` returns `dateOfBirth`, or `null` when it was not given | "stores the date of birth and returns it", "returns null when no date of birth was given" |
+| A date of birth in the future is rejected with an error | "rejects a date of birth in the future", "accepts today as the date of birth" |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** `registerPerson({ email, givenName, familyName, dateOfBirth?, brand? })`; `Person.dateOfBirth: string | null`; new export `InvalidDateOfBirthError`; table row `identity.person` gets `date_of_birth`; new invariant on the date of birth.
+- **Contracts:** none. The `identity.person-registered` payload does not change.
+- **Schema:** `identity.person.date_of_birth`, PostgreSQL `date`, nullable. Personal: yes, category `identity` (existing category, so trigger 3 does not apply), purpose "Identify the person when they give it at registration", owner `identity`, retention `account lifetime + 3 years` (default for account data).
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- "In the future" means after today's business date in `Europe/Berlin` (`kernel.businessDate`), the calendar of the platform. Today is accepted.
+- A value that is not a real `YYYY-MM-DD` calendar date (for example `1990-02-30`) is also rejected with `InvalidDateOfBirthError`.
+- The column is nullable; existing rows get `null`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- A minimum age, a plausibility limit for old dates, and changing the date of birth after registration.
+- Adding the date of birth to an event or to the ERP customer data.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- The data protection officer confirms the purpose of `date_of_birth`. The request did not state why the platform keeps it.
+- Jira key and AC ID for this requirement. When they exist, rename the folder to `docs/specs/AN-<n>/` and prefix the test titles with the AC ID.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
